DevOps Interview Command Series — SonarQube (Day 7) 🔍

SonarQube is a code quality & security gatekeeper in modern CI/CD pipelines.
It helps teams catch bugs, vulnerabilities, and code smells before production.

If you’re preparing for DevOps / SRE / Cloud interviews, these are the SonarQube commands & essentials you must know:

sonar-scanner -v

sonar-scanner \
-Dsonar.projectKey=my-project \
-Dsonar.sources=. \
-Dsonar.host.url=http://sonarqube_url \
-Dsonar.login=SONAR_TOKEN

mvn sonar:sonar

gradle sonarqube

curl -u token: http://sonarqube_url/api/projects/search
curl -u token: http://sonarqube_url/api/issues/search
curl -u token: http://sonarqube_url/api/qualitygates/project_status?projectKey=my-project

systemctl start sonarqube
systemctl status sonarqube
systemctl restart sonarqube

tail -f logs/sonar.log
tail -f logs/web.log
tail -f logs/ce.log


